{"type":"npc","name":"Skyheart","folder":"gtfya5QlMXbZtjD2","system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":320,"temp":0,"max":320,"details":""},"ac":{"value":35,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"Seize Flight"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","pyric","spirituan","sussuran","talican"],"details":""},"level":{"value":14},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>For almost as long as these people have dreamed of soaring through the skies, inventors have sought ways to fuse air magic into solid objects, making devices to allow anyone to experience the wonders of flight. Skyhearts are spirits born from the most successful of these attempts. If their creators managed to fly briefly but failed to sustain that flight, skyhearts could be spirits of collective hope unrealized, able to go airborne temporarily through sheer willpower. Alternatively, they might be relics of a lost civilization left to rust away, able to fly in the ancient past but no longer.</p><p>The physical forms of skyhearts are shambling mechanical masses some 15 feet tall, magical marvels of air, fire, and metal. They want nothing more than to become capable of sustained flight. Some follow at the heels of mages who can briefly grant their wish through magic. Others repeatedly ascend and leap off cliffs and mountains. Still others strive to invent some way to stay aloft through their own ingenuity.</p><hr /><p>Elemental spirits are spiritual beings who embody one or more elements, though those of composite elements tend to be more complex existences.</p><h2>Science Fantasy Settings</h2><p>In high-tech settings, skyhearts might be created through a hybrid of magic and technology or through technology alone. They might be powered by an intentionally created artificial intelligence or an emergent \"ghost in the machine.\" Visually, they might look more like airplanes or spacecraft than magical airships. For such advanced skyhearts, consider reflavoring their abilities to match the vessel's appearance (for example, replacing their fuel spittle with a rocket launcher or laser beam).</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 560/1,250/2,300 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (heavy), shield, perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Crafting)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, body, bane, burning barbs, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (spirit, vitality, void), fire, fire shield, metal, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spirit, strength, sturdy, throwing, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Lachlan Carlsson-Forbes","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":25,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":20,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":24},"athletics":{"base":28},"crafting":{"base":22}},"traits":{"value":["construct","spirit"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"jPkF2iFr6yMXA9sf","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/skyheart.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skyheart","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":3,"height":3,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/skyheart.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/skyheart.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Seize Flight","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The skyheart falls</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The skyheart is at least 10 feet above ground</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The skyheart attempts a @Check[will|dc:30] save.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The skyheart ceases falling, then gains a fly speed of 60 feet and Flies in place. This fly speed lasts for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> Treat the skyheart's fall as up to 240 feet shorter.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The skyheart falls normally.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["air","arcane","concentrate","emotion","mental"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"RiJNSlDsRXvg7JwT","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Turbine Vulnerability","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>An adjacent creature can attempt to disrupt one of the skyheart's two magical turbines with [[/act disable-device dc=37]]. On a success, the skyheart is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.dfCMdR4wnpbYNTix]{Stunned 1}. On a critical failure, the skyheart immediately attempts a turbine Strike; this Strike neither applies nor counts toward the skyheart's multiple attack penalty. If both turbines are disabled, the skyheart can't use turbine Strikes until they spend 10 minutes Repairing themself.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[{"key":"Weakness","type":"custom","definition":["fall-damage"],"value":25,"label":"PF2E.IWR.Custom.FallDamage"}],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"0jhAX0eSDQJd1kyG","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"img":"icons/tools/smithing/anvil.webp","name":"Repair Toolkit (Superb)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A repair kit allows you to perform simple repairs while traveling. It contains a portable anvil, tongs, woodworking tools, a whetstone, and oils for conditioning leather and wood. You can use a repair kit to Repair items using the Crafting skill. A superb repair kit gives you a +1 item bonus to the check. You can draw and replace a worn repair toolkit as part of the action that uses it.</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","label":"Repair Kit, Superb (Repair)","predicate":["action:repair"],"selector":"crafting","type":"item","value":1}],"slug":"repair-toolkit-superb","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":null,"bulk":{"value":1},"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"hardness":0,"price":{"value":{"gp":25}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"containerId":null,"size":"huge","material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"","img":"","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"usage":{"value":"held-in-two-hands"},"subitems":[]},"type":"equipment","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.aDsdYMPpVc8hOnM5","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"S0lyOwoZo1hADqN6"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/FreeAction.webp","name":"Improved Grab","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ImprovedGrab]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"improved-grab","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.i18TlebMzwONyPhI","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"0fcvVINHwLJGQZS6"},{